## 1. Activate the venv

dependency-generator already created `<repo>/.venv/` with everything the RL scripts need (`stable_baselines3[extra]`, `wandb`, `tensorboardX`, `imageio[ffmpeg]`, `matplotlib`, `hydra-core`, `omegaconf`). All you have to do is activate it:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

## 2. Train a policy

The training entry is `harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py` — Hydra-driven, picks up `harbor/configs/rl/<algo>{{PARALLEL_SUFFIX}}.yaml` for defaults and overlays user CLI overrides.

```bash
# Default budget (config), default task ({{DEFAULT_TASK}})
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}}

# Different algorithm, longer training
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=sac task=<task_id> total_timesteps=5_000_000

# Fast smoke (few seconds, W&B off)
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} \
    total_timesteps=5000 wandb=null
```

`gpu_sim={{GPU_SIM}}` for this benchmark, so train.py uses the **{{ENV_FACTORY_MODE}}** env factory ({{ENV_FACTORY_DESCRIPTION}}) and reads `harbor/configs/rl/<algo>{{PARALLEL_SUFFIX}}.yaml`. To force the other path one-off, override `gpu_sim=true` (or `false`) on the CLI.

Outputs land in `<repo>/harbor/outputs/<algo>_<task_slug>_<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>/`:
- `checkpoint.{{CHECKPOINT_EXT}}` — algorithm checkpoint
- `tb/` — TensorBoard event files (`tensorboard --logdir outputs/`)
- `metrics.jsonl` — one JSON record per metric write (step, key, value)
- `curves/*.png` — training curves auto-plotted at end of training (one PNG per metric key)
- `train.log` — stdout mirror
- `resolved_config.yaml` — Hydra config snapshot
- `render.mp4` + `render_contact_sheet.jpg` — written by render.py (after training)

## 3. Evaluate a checkpoint

`harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/eval.py` is **always headless** and uses the **same vec/parallel env** as train.py (so policy obs/action shapes match). Loads the checkpoint, runs `n_episodes` deterministic rollouts, prints aggregate metrics, writes `metrics.json` next to the checkpoint.

```bash
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/eval.py \
    --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} \
    checkpoint=outputs/<trial_id>/checkpoint.{{CHECKPOINT_EXT}} \
    n_episodes=10
```

## 4. Render a trained policy

`harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/render.py` is **always single env** (n=1) with offscreen rendering enabled. Loads the checkpoint, runs ONE episode, writes:

- `<checkpoint-dir>/render.mp4`
- `<checkpoint-dir>/render_contact_sheet.jpg` (5-frame sample)

Works on headless hosts because it uses `render_mode='rgb_array'`. To open a live window, use the env's native viewer (e.g. `dm_control.viewer.launch`, `IsaacLab` standalone scripts, etc.).

```bash
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/render.py \
    --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} \
    checkpoint=outputs/<trial_id>/checkpoint.{{CHECKPOINT_EXT}}
```

## 5. Override hyperparameters

All `harbor/configs/rl/<algo>{{PARALLEL_SUFFIX}}.yaml` fields are Hydra-overridable from the CLI. Common patterns:

```bash
# Different learning rate + longer training
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} \
    learning_rate=1e-4 total_timesteps=10_000_000

# Wider network
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=sac task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} \
    policy_kwargs.net_arch=[512,512,512]

# More parallel envs (CPU vec-env path; raise n_envs cautiously per benchmark)
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} n_envs=16

# Disable W&B for one run
python harbor/scripts/rl/{{ALGORITHM_SLUG}}/train.py --config-name=ppo task={{DEFAULT_TASK}} wandb=null
```

For changes you want to keep, edit `harbor/configs/rl/<algo>.local.yaml` (created on demand; gitignored if you wish) and Hydra will overlay it. **Do not** edit `harbor/configs/rl/<algo>.yaml` directly — `rl-integration-generator` overwrites it on every re-run.

